103 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 17 0 R
/E ( Future work may focus on developing structure-aware generative methods \(segmentation-based or diffusion models etc.\) and expanding the dataset to include a broader range of houseplant species and disease types under diversity background. Improving the visual quality of generated images plays a crucial role, as it directly affects model performance. Exploring domain adaptation and self-supervised learning techniques may further reduce the reliance on large annotated datasets. In parallel, generative methods should accurately replicate key morphological characteristics of houseplants while incorporating diverse backgrounds, camera angles, and lighting conditions to better reflect real-world scenarios. Lastly, deploying models in practical settings and collecting user feedback \(e.g., via mobile or edge devices\) will be essential for validating their real-life applicability.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [85]
>>
endobj
